#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0290 expect=skipped domain=EX
#note "Scope.Classes.Include is [FINDINGS] and the declared class is INTERVENTIONS, so the harness pre-gate reports 'class INTERVENTIONS not in Scope.Classes.Include [FINDINGS]' and the rule never runs -- even though the three rows carry a REAL one-to-many defect. The class= declaration is LOAD-BEARING: without it the SDTM arm of the class gate returns null, the rule RUNS and this data FIRES. expect=skipped is the honest contract; the harness refuses expect=noViolation here."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset EX class=INTERVENTIONS label="Exposure"
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col EXSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col EXTRT    type=Char label="Name of Treatment"
col EXDOSE   type=Num  label="Dose"
col EXTPT    type=Char label="Planned Time Point Name"
col EXTPTNUM type=Num  label="Planned Time Point Number"
---
S1 | EX | 001 | 1 | DRUG X | 10 | 1 HOUR | 1
S1 | EX | 002 | 1 | DRUG X | 10 | 1 HOUR | 2
S1 | EX | 003 | 1 | DRUG X | 10 | 2 HOUR | 3
---
